# Round XII Track P (LHS annotation) + Track R (call-expression) —
# NAMED-binding form `Guard[Speaker] g = m.lock(); g.greet()` (bare trait
# as Mutex inner) is REJECTED at check with `E_NonDerefContainerBareTrait`
# at the LHS `Mutex[Speaker]` annotation. Track R's up-front call-site
# reject has a no-double-report gate so this shape emits ONE error at the
# annotation, not two (verified as a Track R integration probe).
#
# Kept under `known_gaps/` (rather than promoted to top-level) because the
# paired `speaker.gg` module keeps the reject on the Guard-wrapper type
# rather than an accidental same-file resolution shortcut. `main_box.gg`
# (the class-2b Box sibling) graduated out in Round XII Track N2 to
# `tests/fixtures/guard_trait_named_box_dispatch/main.gg`.

from speaker import Speaker, Robot

void main():
    Mutex[Speaker] m = Mutex[Speaker](Robot("R2"))
    Guard[Speaker] g = m.lock()
    print(g.greet())
